<article class="env-lemma" id="06SQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06SQ">Lemma <span data-tag="06SQ">90.10.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a category cofibered in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}_\Lambda $. Let $x_0 \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{F}(k))$. Let $\mathcal{F}_{x_0}$ be the category cofibred in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}_\Lambda $ constructed in Remark <a href="/tag/06GU" data-tag="06GU">90.6.4</a>. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $\mathcal{F}$ satisfies (S1), then so does $\mathcal{F}_{x_0}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $\mathcal{F}$ satisfies (S2), then so does $\mathcal{F}_{x_0}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Any diagram as in Definition <a href="/tag/06HW" data-tag="06HW">90.10.1</a> in $\mathcal{F}_{x_0}$ gives rise to a diagram in $\mathcal{F}$ and the output of condition (S1) or (S2) for this diagram in $\mathcal{F}$ can be viewed as an output for $\mathcal{F}_{x_0}$ as well. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>